  "worked_solution": "We multiply each term inside the parentheses by the term outside the parentheses, simplify using the rules of exponents, and then we add the results together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{p}^{4}(-7{p}^{5}{q}^{2}+3{p}^{2}{q}^{5}) & = \\\\ (-{p}^{4})(-7{p}^{5}{q}^{2})+(-{p}^{4})(3{p}^{2}{q}^{5}) & = \\\\ (\\,(-1)\\cdot (-7)\\,)({p}^{4}\\cdot {p}^{5})({q}^{2})+(\\,(-1)\\cdot 3)({p}^{4}\\cdot {p}^{2})({q}^{5}) & = \\\\ (7)({p}^{4+5})({q}^{2})+(-3)({p}^{4+2})({q}^{5}) & = \\\\ 7{p}^{9}{q}^{2}-3{p}^{6}{q}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
